  closure sees p.a
  dropping closure
  drop p.a
  p.b still usable: p.b
  end of part1
  drop p.b
part2: closure consumes one field
  before call
  took q.b
  drop q.b
  after call, q.a = q.a
  drop q.a
part3: nested field paths
  tag t n 11
  d.inner.b still here: d.inner.b
  moved-in d.inner.a
  after dropping mv
  t!
  drop d.inner.a
  drop d.inner.b
part4: closures in a loop with move
  drop i0
  drop i1
  drop i2
  built 3 closures
  ["i0", "i1", "i2"]
  removed one
  end of part4
part5: FnOnce moving captured whole struct vs field
